Subject: [PATCH 2/3] pdfium: provide the portable font platform on AROS

Reuse PDFium's FreeType/folder-font PlatformIface on AROS so the embedded PDF engine has a concrete graphics-environment module without importing an OS window system.

AI_PHASE: chromium-shared-cef

AI_STATUS: exact-link-gap-fixed-under-validation

AI_VALIDATION: registered native link contained exactly one unresolved CFX_GEModule::PlatformIface::Create symbol

AI_ASSUMPTION: missing Unix font directories safely fall back to PDFium's bundled fonts; AROS FONTS: discovery is a later provider improvement

AI_LIMITATIONS: compile, PDF rendering, and native CEF link remain pending

AI_EVIDENCE: aros-opal-hosted-clean/test-artifacts/-cef-zero-v8-native-link-20260725/04-undefined-symbols.txt

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:
